From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ROG5 Linux Project <rog5-linux@localhost>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom: qmp-ufs: isolate first symbol clock

Generation 38 reproduced target USB loss after entering fixed-rate symbol-clock
registration. Advance the RAM-only SM8350 discriminator through allocation and
only the first fixed-rate clock registration, then stop before the second and
third registrations or OF provider publication.

The UFS core and host remain absent, so this diagnostic cannot enumerate or
access storage.

Signed-off-by: ROG5 Linux Project <rog5-linux@localhost>
---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-ufs.c | 10 +++++-----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-ufs.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-ufs.c
index 0b8ecd336..d724975de 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-ufs.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-ufs.c
@@ -2095,6 +2095,10 @@ static int qmp_ufs_register_clocks(struct qmp_ufs *qmp, struct device_node *np)
 
 	clk_data->hws[0] = hw;
 
+	if (of_device_is_compatible(qmp->dev->of_node,
+				    "qcom,sm8350-qmp-ufs-phy"))
+		return 0;
+
 	snprintf(name, sizeof(name), "%s::rx_symbol_1", dev_name(qmp->dev));
 	hw = devm_clk_hw_register_fixed_rate(qmp->dev, name, NULL, 0, 0);
 	if (IS_ERR(hw))
@@ -2109,10 +2113,6 @@ static int qmp_ufs_register_clocks(struct qmp_ufs *qmp, struct device_node *np)
 
 	clk_data->hws[2] = hw;
 
-	if (of_device_is_compatible(qmp->dev->of_node,
-				    "qcom,sm8350-qmp-ufs-phy"))
-		return 0;
-
 	ret = of_clk_add_hw_provider(np, of_clk_hw_onecell_get, clk_data);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
@@ -2244,7 +2244,7 @@ static int qmp_ufs_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node,
 				    "qcom,sm8350-qmp-ufs-phy")) {
 		dev_notice(dev,
-			   "ROG5 QMP-UFS diagnostic: fixed-rate symbol clocks stage complete\n");
+			   "ROG5 QMP-UFS diagnostic: first fixed-rate symbol clock stage complete\n");
 		of_node_put(np);
 		return 0;
 	}
-- 
2.50.1

